window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-096.json",{"day":96,"title":"The Work Behind a Reliable Town","targetWords":[{"word":"profession","gloss":"行业","context":"When a violent storm damaged the town's water system, the mayor asked each profession to explain what it could contribute.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"coach","gloss":"教练","context":"The headmaster opened the school as a meeting place; a tutor and a coach organized activities for children.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"soldier","gloss":"士兵","context":"A retired soldier worked beside a young fireman, while a veteran carpenter built temporary barriers.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"chairman","gloss":"主席","context":"At headquarters, the chairman of the recovery committee insisted that personnel should be assigned according to real skills, not social status.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"occupation","gloss":"职业","context":"The response revealed how little residents usually knew about one another's occupation.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"personnel","gloss":"人员","context":"At headquarters, the chairman of the recovery committee insisted that personnel should be assigned according to real skills, not social status.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"tutor","gloss":"家教","context":"The headmaster opened the school as a meeting place; a tutor and a coach organized activities for children.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"clerk","gloss":"办事员","context":"A clerk prepared a memorandum describing priorities, and a spokesman corrected a false report about contamination.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"pilot","gloss":"飞行员","context":"The deputy responsible for transport contacted a pilot who could inspect isolated roads from the air.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"pioneer","gloss":"开拓者","context":"The new committee compared its plans with those of its predecessor and asked a pioneer of local training to design practical courses.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"entrepreneur","gloss":"企业家","context":"The town's entrepreneur offered storage space, while a merchant arranged supplies.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"servant","gloss":"仆人","context":"Nobody was expected to treat service as a lifelong vocation or act as an unpaid servant.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"architect","gloss":"建筑师","context":"A plumber inspected broken pipes, an architect assessed weakened roofs, and a mechanic repaired emergency vehicles.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"chef","gloss":"厨师","context":"A grocer supplied food, a butcher organized refrigerated storage, and a chef prepared meals for volunteers.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"mechanic","gloss":"机修工","context":"A plumber inspected broken pipes, an architect assessed weakened roofs, and a mechanic repaired emergency vehicles.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"salesman","gloss":"推销员","context":"A salesman found affordable replacement tools, a tailor repaired protective clothing, and a barber offered free services at a temporary shelter.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"tailor","gloss":"裁缝","context":"A salesman found affordable replacement tools, a tailor repaired protective clothing, and a barber offered free services at a temporary shelter.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"spy","gloss":"间谍","context":"A rumor that a volunteer was a spy briefly threatened cooperation, illustrating how fear can overwhelm evidence.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"mayor","gloss":"市长","context":"When a violent storm damaged the town's water system, the mayor asked each profession to explain what it could contribute.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"practitioner","gloss":"从业者","context":"A dentist and another health practitioner examined people who could not reach their usual clinics.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"dentist","gloss":"牙科医生","context":"A dentist and another health practitioner examined people who could not reach their usual clinics.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"subordinate","gloss":"下属","context":"Respect for expertise meant knowing when to lead and when to become another worker's subordinate.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"crew","gloss":"全体船员","context":"A ship's captain offered help for the coastal settlement, and the crew delivered supplies under the guidance of a steward.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"deputy","gloss":"副手","context":"The deputy responsible for transport contacted a pilot who could inspect isolated roads from the air.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"veteran","gloss":"经验丰富的","context":"A retired soldier worked beside a young fireman, while a veteran carpenter built temporary barriers.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"broker","gloss":"经纪人","context":"An attorney reviewed emergency contracts, while a broker helped businesses understand insurance claims.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"spokesman","gloss":"发言人","context":"A clerk prepared a memorandum describing priorities, and a spokesman corrected a false report about contamination.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"predecessor","gloss":"前任","context":"The new committee compared its plans with those of its predecessor and asked a pioneer of local training to design practical courses.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"administer","gloss":"实施","context":"This cooperation required clear limits: military experience did not automatically make someone qualified to administer medical care or operate local equipment.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"attorney","gloss":"律师","context":"An attorney reviewed emergency contracts, while a broker helped businesses understand insurance claims.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"merchant","gloss":"商人","context":"The town's entrepreneur offered storage space, while a merchant arranged supplies.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"layoff","gloss":"裁员","context":"A threatened layoff could undo a family's progress even after the streets were repaired.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"carpenter","gloss":"木匠","context":"A retired soldier worked beside a young fireman, while a veteran carpenter built temporary barriers.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"barber","gloss":"理发师","context":"A salesman found affordable replacement tools, a tailor repaired protective clothing, and a barber offered free services at a temporary shelter.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"captain","gloss":"船长","context":"A ship's captain offered help for the coastal settlement, and the crew delivered supplies under the guidance of a steward.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"fireman","gloss":"消防队员","context":"A retired soldier worked beside a young fireman, while a veteran carpenter built temporary barriers.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"memorandum","gloss":"备忘录","context":"A clerk prepared a memorandum describing priorities, and a spokesman corrected a false report about contamination.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"ambassador","gloss":"大使","context":"An ambassador from a partner city arranged additional equipment.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"butcher","gloss":"肉商","context":"A grocer supplied food, a butcher organized refrigerated storage, and a chef prepared meals for volunteers.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"steward","gloss":"船上事务员","context":"A ship's captain offered help for the coastal settlement, and the crew delivered supplies under the guidance of a steward.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"vocation","gloss":"使命感","context":"Nobody was expected to treat service as a lifelong vocation or act as an unpaid servant.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"cashier","gloss":"收银员","context":"The cashier recorded payments carefully, because goodwill was no excuse for missing accounts.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"grocer","gloss":"食品店主","context":"A grocer supplied food, a butcher organized refrigerated storage, and a chef prepared meals for volunteers.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"plumber","gloss":"管道工","context":"A plumber inspected broken pipes, an architect assessed weakened roofs, and a mechanic repaired emergency vehicles.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"headmaster","gloss":"校长","context":"The headmaster opened the school as a meeting place; a tutor and a coach organized activities for children.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"shepherd","gloss":"牧羊人","context":"A shepherd moved animals away from flooded fields.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"colonel","gloss":"上校","context":"Even a colonel visiting the area followed civilian instructions.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"headquarters","gloss":"总部","context":"At headquarters, the chairman of the recovery committee insisted that personnel should be assigned according to real skills, not social status.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"world","gloss":"世界","context":"In a world of specialized careers, cooperation succeeds when useful work receives both recognition and the material conditions needed to continue.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"water","gloss":"水","context":"When a violent storm damaged the town's water system, the mayor asked each profession to explain what it could contribute.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"When a violent storm damaged the town's water system, the mayor asked each profession to explain what it could contribute. The response revealed how little residents usually knew about one another's occupation. A plumber inspected broken pipes, an architect assessed weakened roofs, and a mechanic repaired emergency vehicles. The town's entrepreneur offered storage space, while a merchant arranged supplies. At headquarters, the chairman of the recovery committee insisted that personnel should be assigned according to real skills, not social status. A community that appeared divided by job titles began to recognize how closely its daily security depended on shared labor.","zh":"猛烈暴风雨损坏了城镇供水系统，市长请各行业说明可以提供什么帮助。回应显示，居民平时对彼此的职业了解很少。水管工检查破裂管道，建筑师评估受损屋顶，机修工修复应急车辆。企业家提供储存空间，商人组织物资。恢复委员会主席在指挥部强调，人员分工应依据真实技能，而不是社会地位。看似被职业头衔分隔的社区，开始认识日常安全与共同劳动的紧密联系。"},{"en":"The deputy responsible for transport contacted a pilot who could inspect isolated roads from the air. A ship's captain offered help for the coastal settlement, and the crew delivered supplies under the guidance of a steward. A retired soldier worked beside a young fireman, while a veteran carpenter built temporary barriers. Even a colonel visiting the area followed civilian instructions. This cooperation required clear limits: military experience did not automatically make someone qualified to administer medical care or operate local equipment. Respect for expertise meant knowing when to lead and when to become another worker's subordinate.","zh":"负责交通的副手联系飞行员，从空中检查偏僻道路。船长提出帮助沿海聚落，船员在船上事务员协调下运送物资。退役士兵与年轻消防员并肩工作，经验丰富的木匠搭建临时围挡。即使恰好来访的上校，也遵循民事部门指令。合作需要明确边界：军事经验并不自动让人具备实施医疗或操作地方设备的资格。尊重专业意味着知道何时领导、何时听从别人的指挥。"},{"en":"Ordinary businesses became part of the recovery network. A grocer supplied food, a butcher organized refrigerated storage, and a chef prepared meals for volunteers. The cashier recorded payments carefully, because goodwill was no excuse for missing accounts. A salesman found affordable replacement tools, a tailor repaired protective clothing, and a barber offered free services at a temporary shelter. A shepherd moved animals away from flooded fields. A dentist and another health practitioner examined people who could not reach their usual clinics. Their efforts showed that public resilience rests on familiar services as well as extraordinary acts of bravery.","zh":"日常商铺也加入恢复网络。食品店主供应食物，肉商安排冷藏，厨师为志愿者做饭。收银员仔细记录支出，因为好心不能成为账目不清的理由。销售员寻找价格合理的替换工具，裁缝修补防护衣，理发师在临时安置点免费服务。牧羊人把牲畜赶离被淹农田。牙医与另一位医疗从业者检查无法前往原有诊所的人。公共韧性不仅依靠非凡勇气，也依靠这些熟悉的服务。"},{"en":"Communication proved equally important. A clerk prepared a memorandum describing priorities, and a spokesman corrected a false report about contamination. An attorney reviewed emergency contracts, while a broker helped businesses understand insurance claims. The headmaster opened the school as a meeting place; a tutor and a coach organized activities for children. An ambassador from a partner city arranged additional equipment. A rumor that a volunteer was a spy briefly threatened cooperation, illustrating how fear can overwhelm evidence. The committee published decisions openly so that uncertainty would not be filled by suspicion or by exaggerated promises.","zh":"沟通同样重要。办事员准备备忘录说明重点，发言人纠正关于污染的不实报道。律师审查应急合同，经纪人帮助企业理解保险索赔。校长开放学校作为会议场地，家教和教练为孩子组织活动。友好城市的大使安排更多设备。一则声称志愿者是间谍的谣言曾短暂威胁合作，说明恐惧可能压倒证据。委员会公开决策，避免人们用怀疑或夸大承诺填补信息空白。"},{"en":"After recovery, officials discussed how to protect workers whose businesses had closed. A threatened layoff could undo a family's progress even after the streets were repaired. The new committee compared its plans with those of its predecessor and asked a pioneer of local training to design practical courses. Nobody was expected to treat service as a lifelong vocation or act as an unpaid servant. The town had learned that a reliable community must support those who support it. In a world of specialized careers, cooperation succeeds when useful work receives both recognition and the material conditions needed to continue.","zh":"恢复后，官员讨论怎样保护商铺停业的劳动者。即使街道修好了，面临裁员仍可能毁掉一个家庭的生活进展。新委员会比较自身计划与前任计划，请当地职业培训的开拓者设计实用课程。没有人必须把服务当成终身使命，也不应被当成无偿仆人。城镇认识到，可靠社区必须支持那些支撑社区的人。在职业高度专业化的世界里，有用劳动既得到认可，也获得持续所需的物质条件，合作才会成功。"}],"previous":95,"next":97});
